      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved test. The main issues are: unused imports, an unused `DELTA` constant, and bare `assertTrue` calls without descriptive failure messages.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed the unused `DELTA` constant and its comment, removed unused imports (`assertArrayEquals`, `assertNotEquals`, `assertNotNull`), extracted the magic numbers `33` and `42` into named variables (`startInclusive`, `endExclusive`) to clarify their role, and added descriptive failure messages to both `assertTrue` calls so a failing assertion immediately conveys which boundary was violated."
